#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:1
msgid "ADR-0019: Security model of the public instance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:5
msgid ""
"**Plan step**: P14.2, P14.3 (REQ-WEB-9, REQ-WEB-10, REQ-MCP-4, NF-7); the"
" plan calls it \"ADR-0008\", a number already used by \"GPU memory "
"sharing\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:8
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:10
msgid ""
"LUMOS will run as a public instance on a VPS (UC5: students and the "
"general public), and on the machines of its users, where it may drive "
"optical equipment. A public instance must resist anonymous abuse "
"(computations that exhaust the server, guessing passwords) and must never"
" let anyone drive equipment unless an administrator decided it and the "
"person is authenticated. The local instance must not be reachable from "
"other machines or from other web sites open in the same browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:16
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:18
msgid ""
"**Two profiles.** `local` listens on `127.0.0.1` only (refused "
"otherwise); its user is an operator, every action on equipment still "
"needs a confirmation in the interface. `public` serves anonymous visitors"
" as simulators (configurable: viewers, or nobody without login) with "
"quotas; the operation is disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:21
msgid ""
"**Enabling the operation off the local machine** (configuration "
"`operation_enabled`) is refused at start-up unless TLS is set up "
"(certificate, or a reverse proxy terminating TLS with `trust_proxy`), at "
"least one user is an operator and anonymous visitors are not operators. "
"Logging in and operating outside the local machine are refused over plain"
" HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:25
msgid ""
"**Roles**: `viewer` (read, load presets, export), `simulator` (+ edit, "
"run, inspect, simulated actions), `operator` (+ discover and associate "
"devices, actions on equipment). Each route declares the role it needs; "
"the role comes from the server-side session only, never from the request."
" The emergency stop is allowed to every role."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:29
msgid ""
"**Users** are listed in a TOML file managed by `lumos users`: role, "
"Argon2id hash of the password (`argon2-cffi`, never the password), public"
" SSH keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:31
msgid ""
"**SSH keys** prove their owner by signing a server challenge with `ssh-"
"keygen -Y sign -n lumos` (SSHSIG, namespace `lumos`), done by `lumos "
"login` or pasted in the interface. Challenges are random, bound to the "
"user name, valid for 2 minutes and consumed by the first attempt, "
"successful or not (no replay). Ed25519, ECDSA and RSA (SHA-2) signatures "
"are verified with `cryptography`; SHA-1 RSA signatures are refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:35
msgid ""
"**Sessions**: opaque random tokens (cookie `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Strict`,"
" `Secure` over HTTPS, or `Authorization: Bearer` for scripts), renewed at"
" login (no fixation), closed after an idle time and, once authenticated, "
"after a maximum lifetime. Wrong credentials give one message whatever was"
" wrong; unknown users cost the same time as known ones and get challenges"
" too (no enumeration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:39
msgid ""
"**Rate limits** per client address (requests) and per address and user "
"name (login attempts), with `Retry-After`; behind a trusted proxy the "
"address is the first `X-Forwarded-For` entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:41
msgid ""
"**Audit journal** (JSON lines, logger `lumos.audit`): logins, logouts, "
"challenges, refusals, rate limits, device discovery, actions on "
"equipment, emergency stops; never passwords, signatures or tokens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:43
msgid ""
"**Quotas** (P14.3) are enforced by the service, so the MCP server shares "
"them: contexts per session, runs at a time, global concurrent runs, run "
"duration, size of grids and estimated memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:46
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:48
msgid ""
"OAuth or an external identity provider: one more service to run for a "
"small group of operators; can be put in front of the instance by the "
"reverse proxy if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:50
msgid ""
"JWT tokens: no server-side revocation at logout; sessions are cheap to "
"keep in memory for one instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:51
msgid ""
"Verifying signatures with `ssh-keygen -Y verify`: needs OpenSSH on the "
"server and an allowed-signers file per attempt; `cryptography` is already"
" present with TLS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:53
msgid ""
"Allowing the operation with passwords over HTTP on a private network: a "
"single misconfiguration would expose equipment; HTTPS is mandatory "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:56
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:58
msgid ""
"An administrator enables the operation with three explicit settings "
"(operation, TLS, operators); a mistake stops the server at start-up with "
"a message saying what is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:60
msgid ""
"Sessions live in the memory of one process: restarting the server logs "
"everybody out, and running several processes needs sticky sessions (not "
"needed for the expected load)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0019-public-instance-security.md:62
msgid ""
"The MCP server over HTTP mounted in the web instance (P14.9) reuses these"
" sessions and roles."
msgstr ""

